    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d388">

                <pb facs="0467" n="355" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg355"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 837.61351/89</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Special Agent in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Consul General Morgan</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Habana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-02-15T12:00:00-05:29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 15, 1918, noon.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>For Hoover, Food Administration:</p>
                <p>I have given wide publicity throughout Cuba to your telegram of February 12, 6
                    p.m., regarding the price of sugar imported into <pb facs="0468" n="356"
                        xml:id="pg356"/> the United States and your success in bringing the loan to
                    a successful issue. The information has been received with great satisfaction
                    here. It will also have a good effect in stopping speculation in sugar in
                    Cuba.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morgan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
